(Note: it does **not** touch the internal `defaultZone` variable, so a previously set default zone survives `resetCaches()`.)

## Answers (verified by running `./node_modules/.bin/babel-node` against src, node v10.24.1)

**1. What does `Settings.defaultZone` return when internal `defaultZone === null`?**
It returns `LocalZone.instance` (line 62, `defaultZone || LocalZone.instance`), a lazily created singleton (`src/zones/localZone.js:15-20`). It is **not** `SystemZone.instance` (that class doesn't exist here) and **not** `null`. Verified: `Settings.defaultZone === LocalZone.instance` → `true`; `constructor.name` → `LocalZone`; `type` → `"local"`; `name` → the runtime zone, `"America/New_York"` in this container (via `Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone`). Because it is a `||` check, any falsy internal value (`null`, `undefined`) yields `LocalZone.instance`.

**2. What does the setter do with `null`?** There is **no setter for `defaultZone`** — only `defaultZoneName` has a setter. Runtime proof:
```
Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(Settings, "defaultZone")     -> { get: [Function: get], set: undefined, ... }
Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(Settings, "defaultZoneName") -> { get: [Function: get], set: [Function: set], ... }
Settings.defaultZone = null  -> TypeError: Cannot set property defaultZone of function Settings() { _classCallCheck(this, Settings); } which has only a getter
```
So `Settings.defaultZone = null` (or `= "UTC"`, or any value) **throws a TypeError** and stores nothing. The supported API is `Settings.defaultZoneName`:
- `Settings.defaultZoneName = null` (or `""`, `undefined`, `false`, `0` — anything falsy, because of `if (!z)`) → stores `defaultZone = null` (line 51). The getter then returns `LocalZone.instance`, i.e. **null is not stored as a zone and never returned; it is converted to LocalZone at read time** (not to SystemZone). Verified: after `defaultZoneName = null`, `Settings.defaultZone === LocalZone.instance` → `true`, `name` → `"America/New_York"`. This is exactly what `test/helpers.js:82-90` `withDefaultZone` relies on for teardown.

**3. String handling via `Settings.defaultZoneName = <string>`** (goes through `normalizeZone`, `src/impl/zoneUtil.js:12-36`):
- `"UTC"` → `FixedOffsetZone.utcInstance` (zoneUtil.js:21 matches `lowered === "utc"`). Verified: `defaultZoneName` → `"UTC"`, ctor `FixedOffsetZone`, `type "fixed"`, `isValid true`, `!== LocalZone.instance`.
- `"local"` → `defaultZone` param is `undefined` here, so `normalizeZone` returns `undefined` (zoneUtil.js:20) → internal variable becomes `undefined` → getter falls back to `LocalZone.instance`. Verified: `defaultZone === LocalZone.instance` → `true`.
